   "title": "The action potential and the all-or-none law",
   "kind": "Simulation",
   "sub": "Stimulate a patch of nerve membrane: below threshold nothing fires, above it every action potential is the same size. Find the threshold and the refractory period that limits firing rate.",
   "note": "SciGradify Biology's simulation: the published Hodgkin–Huxley (1952) equations for squid axon membrane; a motor neurone behaves the same way in principle, with no propagation or myelin modelled.",
